From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 13:46:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-oneplus-iceland: MDSS needs the
 INT2 GDSC as well

The display is powered by both core GDSCs of the display clock controller, as in the stock kernel
(canoe-sde: "core_gdsc", "core_int2_gdsc"). List both on the MDSS node, so the native display keeps
MDSS_CORE_INT2 on after the boot framebuffer is released.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
index 6495b96afe22..96d01ebbae32 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-oneplus-iceland.dts
@@ -1080,6 +1080,13 @@ backlight@11 {
 };
 
 &mdss {
+	/*
+	 * The display needs both core GDSCs, as in the stock kernel (canoe-sde: "core_gdsc", "core_int2_gdsc").
+	 * With INT2 off the DPU stops scanning out even though the KMS reports the panel on.
+	 */
+	power-domains = <&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_CORE_GDSC>,
+			<&dispcc DISP_CC_MDSS_CORE_INT2_GDSC>;
+
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
